# ==============================================================================
# STEP 00: DATA PREPARATION PIPELINE
# Global multi-crop panel: annual climate variables + FAOSTAT yield data
#
# Pipeline overview:
#   Step 1 : CRU TS4.09 + CROPGRIDS -> monthly climate panel     -> panelv1_*
#   Step 2 : Annual aggregation + FAO yield/CO2/GDP join + filters -> panelv2_*
#   Step 3 : Extra countries patch (IRN, EGY, NGA, SDN)          -> panelv3_*
#   Step 4 : FAOSTAT irrigation data                             -> panelv4_*
#   Step 5 : Cropland area + irr_ratio                           -> panelv5_*
#   Step 6 : Aridity Index (year-varying AI/is_arid AND fixed    -> panelv6_*
#            AI_baseline/is_arid_fixed, both AI = PRE_ann/PET_ann)
#   Step 7 : GDP per capita (WDI, backfill fix) + fixed-baseline      -> panelv7_* (final)
#            weighting columns
#            baseline production/area weights
#
# Notes on scope:
#   - No phenology windows. All climate variables are ANNUAL means/sums.
#   - No VPD. Vapour pressure (VAP_ann) is retained only as a general
#     climate control variable, not converted into VPD anywhere.
#   - Aridity is defined using the UNEP (1997) Aridity Index (AI = P/PET),
#     not a raw precipitation threshold. is_arid = 1 if AI < 0.50 (semi-arid
#     and drier). PET data quality is checked explicitly before use.
#   - Two aridity variables exist: AI/is_arid (year-varying, this country's
#     own year) and AI_baseline/is_arid_fixed (time-invariant, from the
#     1990-2000 baseline window or a documented fallback). The fixed
#     version is what the fixed-aridity interaction specification (is_arid_fixed
#     x TMX) uses, so that it measures structural aridity rather than
#     duplicating the within-year precipitation x TMX interaction. The
#     fixed-baseline production/area weights (baseline_production_tonnes,
#     baseline_area_harvested_ha) are computed in Step 7 using the same
#     1990-2000-or-fallback window as the fixed aridity classification --
#     one consistent design for every non-contemporaneous, fixed country
#     characteristic in the pipeline.
#
# Input files (all in base_dir):
#   CRU_TS4.09_*.nc                          -- CRU TS4.09 monthly climate grids
#   CROPGRIDSv1.08_*.nc                      -- CROPGRIDS crop-specific area rasters (circa 2020)
#   Production_Crops_Livestock_E_All_Data_(Normalized).csv -- FAOSTAT
#   GLOBAL_ATMOSPHERIC_CO2_NOAA.csv
#   gdp_per_person.csv                       -- fallback GDP (overridden by WDI in Step 7)
#   FAOSTAT_data_en_3-5-2026.xls             -- FAOSTAT irrigation data
#   sudanvs.xls                              -- FAO data for IRN/EGY/NGA/SDN
#
# Country list: derived directly from FAOSTAT (no separate country-list file).
# A country enters the panel if FAOSTAT records Production or Yield for at
# least one of the eight target crops, 1961-2024, excluding regional
# aggregates. This avoids depending on any previously self-generated file.
#
# Output files: panelv7_wheat.xlsx ... panelv7_sorghum.xlsx
#
# Required packages:
#   install.packages(c("terra","geodata","dplyr","readxl","writexl",
#                      "data.table","tidyr","zoo","rnaturalearth",
